   ["(n+1)x₍ₙ₎/n = 4.9","x₍ₙ₎ = 4.2","2x̄, which cannot be found from this information","n x₍ₙ₎/(n+1) = 3.6"],
   "A","E[X₍₆₎] = 6θ/7, so multiplying by 7/6 gives an unbiased estimator: (n+1)X₍ₙ₎/n = (7/6)(4.2) = 4.9. Option D applies the correction the wrong way round and produces an estimate BELOW the largest observation, which is impossible.",
